---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Pi-hole (Docker) Deployment" description="Project: Pi-hole deployed in Docker - network-wide ad blocking solution">
  <nav>
    <div class="nav-content">
      <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 1rem;">
        <a href="/" class="logo" style="text-decoration: none; cursor: pointer; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.4em;">
          <img src="/favicon.svg" alt="Logo" style="height: 1.7em; width: auto; vertical-align: middle; display: inline-block; margin-left: 0.1em;" />
        </a>
        <a href="/#projects" style="text-decoration: none; color: #00FF8C; font-size: 0.95rem; transition: color 0.3s;">← Back</a>
      </div>
      <div class="hamburger" id="hamburger">
        <span></span>
        <span></span>
        <span></span>
      </div>
      <div class="nav-links" id="navLinks">
        <a href="#overview">Overview</a>
        <a href="#prerequisites">Prerequisites</a>
        <a href="#setup">Setup Steps</a>
        <a href="#troubleshooting">Troubleshooting</a>
        <a href="#resources">Resources</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </nav>

  <section class="hero" id="hero">
    <div class="hero-content" style="display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: flex-start; gap: 2.5rem; max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto;">
      <div style="flex: 1; text-align: left;">
        <h1>Pi-hole Docker Deployment</h1>
        <div class="tag">// Network-wide Ad Blocking</div>
        <p class="subtitle">Deploy Pi-hole in Docker containers for comprehensive network security and ad blocking</p>
      </div>
      <div style="flex: 1; display: flex; justify-content: center;">
        <img src="https://cdn.brandfetch.io/idu5KIKDYg/theme/dark/logo.svg?c=1bxid64Mup7aczewSAYMX&t=1763570042932" alt="Pi-hole Logo" style="height: 280px; width: 280px; border-radius: 12px; background: #fff; padding: 1rem;" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="project-page">
    <!-- Dashboard Banner -->
    <img 
      src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cyber-wpmm/Pi-Hole/main/images/Dashboard.png"
      alt="Pi-hole Dashboard"
      style="
        width: 100%;
        max-width: 100%;
        border-radius: 8px;
        margin-bottom: 2rem;
        box-shadow: 0 4px 12px rgba(0, 255, 140, 0.1);
      "
    />

    <!-- Overview -->
    <section id="overview">
      <h2>Overview</h2>
      <p>This guide covers the complete installation and configuration of Pi-hole on a Raspberry Pi using Docker. It includes:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Setting up a static IP address</li>
        <li>Docker and Docker Compose installation</li>
        <li>Pi-hole container deployment</li>
        <li>Adding comprehensive blocklists</li>
        <li>Client DNS configuration</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- Prerequisites -->
    <section id="prerequisites">
      <h2>Prerequisites</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Raspberry Pi with Linux OS installed (Ubuntu Server or Raspberry Pi OS)</li>
        <li>Valid internet connection (Ethernet or Wi-Fi)</li>
        <li>SSH access to the Pi</li>
        <li>Basic command line knowledge</li>
      </ul>

      <p><strong>Tip:</strong> When using Raspberry Pi Imager, pre-configure Wi-Fi and credentials using <strong>Ctrl + Shift + X</strong> (Windows) or <strong>Command + Shift + X</strong> (macOS) before flashing.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- Setup Guide -->
    <section id="setup">
      <h2>Setup Guide</h2>
      
      <div style="
        background: rgba(0, 255, 140, 0.05);
        border-left: 4px solid var(--accent-color, #00FF8C);
        padding: 1.5rem;
        margin-bottom: 2rem;
        border-radius: 4px;
      ">
        <h3 style="margin-top: 0;">Step 1: Initial Setup and IP Configuration</h3>
        <p><strong>Finding Your Pi's IP Address:</strong></p>
        <p><strong>Option 1 - Through Router:</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>Log into your router's web interface (usually <code>192.168.0.1</code> or <code>192.168.1.1</code>)</li>
          <li>Look for "DHCP Clients" or "Connected Devices"</li>
          <li>Find your Pi's IP address</li>
        </ul>
        <p><strong>Option 2 - Direct Access:</strong></p>
        <pre style="background-color: #1e1e1e; padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 4px; overflow-x: auto; border-left: 4px solid var(--accent-color, #00FF8C); font-size: 1.05em; line-height: 1.6;"><code style="color: #d4d4d4; font-family: 'Courier New', monospace;">ip a
<span style="color: #6a9955;"># or</span>
ifconfig</code></pre>

        <p><strong>Connecting via SSH:</strong></p>
        <pre style="background-color: #1e1e1e; padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 4px; overflow-x: auto; border-left: 4px solid var(--accent-color, #00FF8C); font-size: 1.05em; line-height: 1.6;"><code style="color: #d4d4d4; font-family: 'Courier New', monospace;"><span style="color: #569cd6;">ssh</span> username@ip_address</code></pre>

        <p><strong>Update System:</strong></p>
        <pre style="background-color: #1e1e1e; padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 4px; overflow-x: auto; border-left: 4px solid var(--accent-color, #00FF8C); font-size: 1.05em; line-height: 1.6;"><code style="color: #d4d4d4; font-family: 'Courier New', monospace;"><span style="color: #569cd6;">sudo apt</span> update <span style="color: #569cd6;">&&</span> <span style="color: #569cd6;">sudo apt</span> upgrade -y</code></pre>
      </div>

      <div style="
        background: rgba(0, 255, 140, 0.05);
        border-left: 4px solid var(--accent-color, #00FF8C);
        padding: 1.5rem;
        margin-bottom: 2rem;
        border-radius: 4px;
      ">
        <h3 style="margin-top: 0;">Step 2: Setting Static IP Address</h3>
        <p>A static IP ensures Pi-hole remains accessible at the same address.</p>
        
        <p><strong>Method 1: Ubuntu Server (Using Netplan)</strong></p>
        <pre style="background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3); padding: 1rem; border-radius: 4px; overflow-x: auto;"><code>sudo nano /etc/netplan/50-cloud-init.yaml</code></pre>

        <p><strong>For Ethernet connection (eth0):</strong></p>
        <pre style="background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3); padding: 1rem; border-radius: 4px; overflow-x: auto;"><code>network:
  version: 2
  renderer: networkd
  ethernets:
    eth0:
      dhcp4: no
      addresses: [192.168.10.50/24]
      routes:
        - to: 0.0.0.0/0
          via: 192.168.0.1
      nameservers:
        addresses: [1.1.1.1, 8.8.8.8]</code></pre>

        <p><strong>Apply changes:</strong></p>
        <pre style="background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3); padding: 1rem; border-radius: 4px; overflow-x: auto;"><code>sudo netplan apply
ip a
ping google.com</code></pre>

        <p><strong>Method 2: Raspberry Pi OS (Using NetworkManager)</strong></p>
        <pre style="background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3); padding: 1rem; border-radius: 4px; overflow-x: auto;"><code>nmcli connection show
nmcli connection modify "Wired connection 1" ipv4.addresses 192.168.1.100/24
nmcli connection modify "Wired connection 1" ipv4.gateway 192.168.1.1
nmcli connection modify "Wired connection 1" ipv4.dns "8.8.8.8 1.1.1.1"
nmcli connection modify "Wired connection 1" ipv4.method manual
nmcli connection down "Wired connection 1"
nmcli connection up "Wired connection 1"</code></pre>
      </div>

      <div style="
        background: rgba(0, 255, 140, 0.05);
        border-left: 4px solid var(--accent-color, #00FF8C);
        padding: 1.5rem;
        margin-bottom: 2rem;
        border-radius: 4px;
      ">
        <h3 style="margin-top: 0;">Step 3: Installing Docker</h3>
        <p><strong>Install Docker using the official script:</strong></p>
        <pre style="background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3); padding: 1rem; border-radius: 4px; overflow-x: auto;"><code>curl -fsSL https://get.docker.com -o get-docker.sh
sudo sh get-docker.sh
sudo usermod -aG docker $USER
sudo reboot</code></pre>

        <p><strong>Verify Installation:</strong></p>
        <pre style="background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3); padding: 1rem; border-radius: 4px; overflow-x: auto;"><code>docker --version
docker compose version</code></pre>
      </div>

      <div style="
        background: rgba(0, 255, 140, 0.05);
        border-left: 4px solid var(--accent-color, #00FF8C);
        padding: 1.5rem;
        margin-bottom: 2rem;
        border-radius: 4px;
      ">
        <h3 style="margin-top: 0;">Step 4: Pi-hole Docker Setup</h3>
        <p><strong>Create Pi-hole Directory:</strong></p>
        <pre style="background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3); padding: 1rem; border-radius: 4px; overflow-x: auto;"><code>mkdir ~/pihole
cd ~/pihole</code></pre>

        <p><strong>Create Docker Compose configuration:</strong></p>
        <pre style="background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3); padding: 1rem; border-radius: 4px; overflow-x: auto;"><code>services:
  pihole:
    container_name: pihole
    image: pihole/pihole:latest
    ports:
      - "53:53/tcp"
      - "53:53/udp"
      - "80:80/tcp"
      - "443:443/tcp"
    environment:
      TZ: 'Pacific/Auckland'
      FTLCONF_webserver_api_password: 'YourSecurePassword'
      FTLCONF_dns_listeningMode: 'all'
    volumes:
      - './etc-pihole:/etc/pihole'
      - './etc-dnsmasq.d:/etc/dnsmasq.d'
    restart: unless-stopped</code></pre>

        <p><strong>Start Pi-hole Container:</strong></p>
        <pre style="background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3); padding: 1rem; border-radius: 4px; overflow-x: auto;"><code>docker compose up -d
docker ps</code></pre>

        <p><strong>Access Web Interface:</strong></p>
        <p>Open browser and navigate to: <code>http://192.168.10.50/admin</code> (replace with your Pi's static IP)</p>
      </div>

      <div style="
        background: rgba(0, 255, 140, 0.05);
        border-left: 4px solid var(--accent-color, #00FF8C);
        padding: 1.5rem;
        margin-bottom: 2rem;
        border-radius: 4px;
      ">
        <h3 style="margin-top: 0;">Step 5: Adding Blocklists</h3>
        <p><strong>Method 1: Via SQLite (Bulk Import)</strong></p>
        <pre style="background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3); padding: 1rem; border-radius: 4px; overflow-x: auto;"><code>sudo apt install sqlite3
sudo sqlite3 ~/pihole/etc-pihole/gravity.db

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO adlist (address) VALUES 
('https://raw.githubusercontent.com/StevenBlack/hosts/master/hosts'),
('https://adaway.org/hosts.txt'),
('https://v.firebog.net/hosts/AdguardDNS.txt'),
('https://pgl.yoyo.org/adservers/serverlist.php?hostformat=hosts&showintro=0&mimetype=plaintext'),
('https://raw.githubusercontent.com/anudeepND/blacklist/master/adservers.txt');

.exit
docker exec -it pihole pihole -g</code></pre>

        <p><strong>Method 2: Via Web Interface</strong></p>
        <ol>
          <li>Go to <strong>Adlists</strong> in the web interface</li>
          <li>Add blocklist URLs one by one</li>
          <li>Click <strong>Tools</strong> → <strong>Update Gravity</strong></li>
        </ol>

        <p><strong>Recommended Blocklist Resources:</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="https://github.com/hagezi/dns-blocklists" target="_blank" style="color: var(--accent-color, #00FF8C); text-decoration: underline;">Hagezi DNS Blocklists</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://github.com/r0xd4n3t/pihole-adblock-lists" target="_blank" style="color: var(--accent-color, #00FF8C); text-decoration: underline;">r0xd4n3t's Pi-hole Lists</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://firebog.net/" target="_blank" style="color: var(--accent-color, #00FF8C); text-decoration: underline;">Firebog Blocklists</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div style="
        background: rgba(0, 255, 140, 0.05);
        border-left: 4px solid var(--accent-color, #00FF8C);
        padding: 1.5rem;
        margin-bottom: 2rem;
        border-radius: 4px;
      ">
        <h3 style="margin-top: 0;">Step 6: Configuring DNS Clients</h3>
        <p><strong>Option 1: Configure Router (Recommended)</strong></p>
        <ol>
          <li>Log into router's web interface</li>
          <li>Find <strong>DHCP Settings</strong> or <strong>LAN Settings</strong></li>
          <li>Set <strong>Primary DNS</strong> to Pi's IP address (e.g., <code>192.168.10.50</code>)</li>
          <li>Optionally set <strong>Secondary DNS</strong> to <code>8.8.8.8</code></li>
          <li>Save and reboot router</li>
        </ol>

        <p><strong>Option 2: Configure Individual Devices</strong></p>
        <p><strong>For Windows:</strong></p>
        <ol>
          <li>Open <strong>Network & Internet Settings</strong></li>
          <li>Click <strong>Change adapter options</strong></li>
          <li>Right-click your network → <strong>Properties</strong></li>
          <li>Select <strong>Internet Protocol Version 4 (TCP/IPv4)</strong></li>
          <li>Choose <strong>Use the following DNS server addresses</strong></li>
          <li>Enter Pi's IP: <code>192.168.10.50</code></li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Troubleshooting -->
    <section id="troubleshooting">
      <h2>Troubleshooting</h2>

      <div style="
        background: rgba(255, 100, 100, 0.05);
        border-left: 4px solid #ff6464;
        padding: 1.5rem;
        margin-bottom: 2rem;
        border-radius: 4px;
      ">
        <h3 style="margin-top: 0;">Password Not Working</h3>
        <p>If you can't log in with the password set in docker-compose.yml:</p>
        <pre style="background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3); padding: 1rem; border-radius: 4px; overflow-x: auto;"><code>docker exec -it pihole /bin/bash
pihole setpassword YourNewPassword
exit</code></pre>
      </div>

      <div style="
        background: rgba(255, 100, 100, 0.05);
        border-left: 4px solid #ff6464;
        padding: 1.5rem;
        margin-bottom: 2rem;
        border-radius: 4px;
      ">
        <h3 style="margin-top: 0;">Port 53 Already in Use</h3>
        <pre style="background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3); padding: 1rem; border-radius: 4px; overflow-x: auto;"><code>sudo ss -tulpn | grep :53

# If systemd-resolved is using it
sudo systemctl stop systemd-resolved
sudo systemctl disable systemd-resolved</code></pre>
      </div>

      <div style="
        background: rgba(255, 100, 100, 0.05);
        border-left: 4px solid #ff6464;
        padding: 1.5rem;
        margin-bottom: 2rem;
        border-radius: 4px;
      ">
        <h3 style="margin-top: 0;">Container Won't Start</h3>
        <pre style="background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3); padding: 1rem; border-radius: 4px; overflow-x: auto;"><code>docker logs pihole
docker restart pihole</code></pre>
      </div>

      <div style="
        background: rgba(255, 100, 100, 0.05);
        border-left: 4px solid #ff6464;
        padding: 1.5rem;
        margin-bottom: 2rem;
        border-radius: 4px;
      ">
        <h3 style="margin-top: 0;">DNS Not Working on Clients</h3>
        <pre style="background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3); padding: 1rem; border-radius: 4px; overflow-x: auto;"><code>nslookup google.com 192.168.10.50
docker exec -it pihole pihole -t</code></pre>
      </div>

      <div style="
        background: rgba(255, 100, 100, 0.05);
        border-left: 4px solid #ff6464;
        padding: 1.5rem;
        margin-bottom: 2rem;
        border-radius: 4px;
      ">
        <h3 style="margin-top: 0;">Web Interface Not Accessible</h3>
        <pre style="background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3); padding: 1rem; border-radius: 4px; overflow-x: auto;"><code>docker ps
ip a
curl http://localhost/admin</code></pre>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- What I Have Learned -->
    <section id="resources" style="margin-bottom: 3rem;">
      <h2>What I Have Learned</h2>
      <p>Through this project, I have gained valuable insights into:</p>
      
      <div class="tech-grid">
        <div class="tech-card">
          <strong>Networking Basics</strong>
          <p>Understanding static IP configuration and DNS management.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="tech-card">
          <strong>Docker</strong>
          <p>Setting up and managing containers for efficient application deployment.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="tech-card">
          <strong>Pi-hole</strong>
          <p>Deploying and configuring Pi-hole as a network-wide ad blocker.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="tech-card">
          <strong>Automation</strong>
          <p>Writing scripts to simplify repetitive tasks and manage containers.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="tech-card">
          <strong>Troubleshooting</strong>
          <p>Diagnosing and resolving common issues related to DNS, Docker, and Pi-hole.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="tech-card">
          <strong>System Administration</strong>
          <p>Enhanced skills in scripting and network security.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Additional Resources -->
    <section style="margin-bottom: 3rem;">
      <h2>Additional Resources</h2>
      
      <h3>Official Documentation</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="https://docs.pi-hole.net/" target="_blank" style="color: var(--accent-color, #00FF8C); text-decoration: underline;">Pi-hole Documentation</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://github.com/pi-hole/docker-pi-hole" target="_blank" style="color: var(--accent-color, #00FF8C); text-decoration: underline;">Docker Pi-hole GitHub</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://github.com/cyber-wpmm/Pi-Hole" target="_blank" style="color: var(--accent-color, #00FF8C); text-decoration: underline;">Project Repository</a></li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Blocklist Collections</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="https://github.com/hagezi/dns-blocklists" target="_blank" style="color: var(--accent-color, #00FF8C); text-decoration: underline;">Hagezi DNS Blocklists</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://github.com/r0xd4n3t/pihole-adblock-lists" target="_blank" style="color: var(--accent-color, #00FF8C); text-decoration: underline;">r0xd4n3t's Pi-hole Lists</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://firebog.net/" target="_blank" style="color: var(--accent-color, #00FF8C); text-decoration: underline;">Firebog Blocklists</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://blocklist.site/" target="_blank" style="color: var(--accent-color, #00FF8C); text-decoration: underline;">The Block List Project</a></li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- Useful Commands -->
    <section style="margin-bottom: 3rem;">
      <h2>Useful Commands</h2>
      <pre style="background-color: #1e1e1e; padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 4px; overflow-x: auto; border-left: 4px solid var(--accent-color, #00FF8C); font-size: 1.1em; line-height: 1.6;"><code style="color: #d4d4d4; font-family: 'Courier New', monospace;"><span style="color: #6a9955;"># Update Pi-hole</span>
<span style="color: #569cd6;">docker pull</span> pihole/pihole:latest
<span style="color: #569cd6;">docker compose</span> down
<span style="color: #569cd6;">docker compose</span> up -d

<span style="color: #6a9955;"># View live query log</span>
<span style="color: #569cd6;">docker exec</span> -it pihole pihole -t

<span style="color: #6a9955;"># Update gravity</span>
<span style="color: #569cd6;">docker exec</span> -it pihole pihole -g

<span style="color: #6a9955;"># Restart DNS service</span>
<span style="color: #569cd6;">docker exec</span> -it pihole pihole restartdns

<span style="color: #6a9955;"># Check Pi-hole status</span>
<span style="color: #569cd6;">docker exec</span> -it pihole pihole status</code></pre>
    </section>

    <!-- Scroll to Top Button -->
    <button id="scrollToTopBtn" style="
      position: fixed;
      bottom: 2rem;
      right: 2rem;
      background-color: var(--accent-color, #00FF8C);
      color: #000;
      border: none;
      border-radius: 50%;
      width: 50px;
      height: 50px;
      font-size: 1.5rem;
      cursor: pointer;
      display: none;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      box-shadow: 0 4px 12px rgba(0, 255, 140, 0.3);
      transition: all 0.3s ease;
      z-index: 1000;
    ">
      ↑
    </button>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  :global(body) {
    color: var(--text-color);
  }

  :global(pre) {
    background-color: #1e1e1e !important;
    padding: 1.5rem !important;
    border-radius: 4px !important;
    overflow-x: auto !important;
    border-left: 4px solid var(--accent-color, #00FF8C) !important;
    font-size: 1.05em !important;
    line-height: 1.6 !important;
  }

  :global(code) {
    color: #d4d4d4 !important;
    font-family: 'Courier New', monospace !important;
    font-size: inherit !important;
  }
</style>

<script>
  const navToggle = document.getElementById('nav-toggle');
  const nav = document.querySelector('nav');
  
  if (navToggle && nav) {
    navToggle.addEventListener('click', () => {
      nav.style.display = nav.style.display === 'none' ? 'flex' : 'none';
    });
  }

  document.querySelectorAll('a[href^="#"]').forEach(anchor => {
    anchor.addEventListener('click', function(e) {
      e.preventDefault();
      const target = document.querySelector(this.getAttribute('href'));
      if (target) {
        target.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth' });
      }
    });
  });

  // Scroll to Top functionality
  const scrollToTopBtn = document.getElementById('scrollToTopBtn');
  
  window.addEventListener('scroll', () => {
    if (window.scrollY > 300) {
      scrollToTopBtn.style.display = 'flex';
    } else {
      scrollToTopBtn.style.display = 'none';
    }
  });

  scrollToTopBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
    window.scrollTo({
      top: 0,
      behavior: 'smooth'
    });
  });
</script>
    